     "id": "n0",
     "set": {
      "text": "loops → AND gates, sum → OR gate"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Put two bubbles on each wire between the levels (a double inversion changes nothing). An AND with an output bubble is a NAND; an OR with input bubbles is, by De Morgan, a NAND.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "g1",
     "set": {
      "kind": "nand"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g2",
     "set": {
      "kind": "nand"
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "g3",
     "set": {
      "bubbles": [
       0,
       1
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "n0",
     "set": {
      "text": "add bubble pairs on the middle wires"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "So the same circuit is three NAND gates: f = NAND(NAND(A′, C), NAND(A, B)). Every SOP becomes NAND–NAND this way; a POS becomes NOR–NOR dually.",
